//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// SaintTrades Rejection Block (ICT / Powell)                           INDICATOR
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Marks rejection blocks the way Powell Trades (Dumb Money Concepts) and ICT
// teach them, trades every one three ways, and measures each setup in a stats
// table, so the chart shows what actually worked on this symbol and timeframe.
// Non-repainting: everything runs on closed bars only.
//
// --------------------------------- RULES -------------------------------------
//  R1. A rejection block (RB) is the WICK of a candle that ran a level and closed
//      back on the other side of it. Bearish: the upper wick trades through the
//      level and the whole body stays below it. Bullish is the mirror image.
//  R2. Levels. Powell key opens (New York time) 00:00 / 02:00 / 08:30 / 09:30 /
//      10:00 / 13:30 / 18:00 are two-sided: a wick can reject them from either
//      side for the rest of the trading day, and a touch is enough. ICT liquidity
//      is one-sided and spent once price trades through it: previous day and
//      week high/low, Asia / London / NY AM session high/low, and swing
//      highs/lows on the RB timeframe.
//  R3. Zone = body edge (the open or close nearest the wick) to the wick tip.
//      CE (consequent encroachment, the "mean threshold") = 50% of the wick.
//      ICT option: when earlier candles wicked into the same area, the zone runs
//      from the body nearest the tip among them to the tip ("highest body to
//      highest wick" for a bearish RB).
//  R4. The rejecting wick must dominate its candle: at least X% of the range,
//      at least Y x the body, longer than the opposite wick, and at least
//      Z x ATR(14) of the RB timeframe, so small wicks are ignored.
//  R5. Invalidation (Powell): any wick past the tip, no close needed.
//      ICT option: a close past the tip.
//  R6. Entries. All three are measured on every RB:
//        CE limit        - Powell's limit at the CE, stop past the tip.
//        Body-edge limit - fills on the first touch of the zone.
//        CISD after tap  - after the first touch, wait for a chart bar to close
//                          back through the open of the run of candles that
//                          pushed into the zone (Powell's entry trigger), and
//                          enter at that close. Powell's stop goes past the
//                          high (low) made after the tap, not past the RB tip.
//  R7. Stop = tip + buffer (CISD: see R6), moved out to a minimum distance from
//      the entry (Powell: about 5 NQ points). TP1 = fixed R. TP2 = fixed R, or
//      the nearest untaken opposing liquidity.
//  R8. Wick theory. An RB whose tip makes equal highs/lows with an earlier
//      candle is not clean: those equal highs/lows are fresh liquidity that tends
//      to get run. Displacement: after the RB, a candle on the RB timeframe
//      should close through the start of the leg that ran into it (CISD) before
//      price comes back to the zone. A fair value gap left by the move away
//      from the RB is a second kind of displacement.
//  R9. SMT. The sweep is stronger when a correlated market (ES for NQ) fails to
//      make the same new high/low: one of the two makes it, the other doesn't.
// R10. Powell's bullish RB closes bullish (bearish closes bearish), and his
//      daily bias is PXH/PXL: the previous day closing beyond the day before's
//      high/low, or sweeping it and closing back inside.
//
// ------------------------------- ASSUMPTIONS ---------------------------------
//  A1. RB-timeframe candles are built from chart bars. A candle is finalized on
//      its last chart bar. If that bar can't be detected (a session break), the
//      candle is finalized on the next bar instead. That RB can't fill on the bar
//      where it was found, and it is dropped if that bar already took its tip.
//  A2. A level counts only if it existed before the RB candle opened and, for
//      one-sided liquidity, price had not traded through it before that candle.
//      Key opens are live from the bar after they print. Day/week/session levels
//      are live from the first bar after their period closes. Swing points are
//      live from the close of the candle that confirms them.
//  A3. Key opens need a chart bar that opens exactly at that time (08:30, 09:30
//      and 13:30 do not exist on a 1H chart). They expire when the New York
//      trading day rolls at 18:00, or at the daily bar change on a market with
//      no bar at 18:00 NY.
//  A4. One RB per zone: a wick that stays inside a live RB of the same direction
//      is a retest of that RB, not a new one. With "Highest body in swing", the
//      cluster is up to 5 candles right before the RB whose wicks reached its
//      body and not past its tip; only candles that already closed count.
//  A5. Fills are conservative. A limit fills on a bar after the RB is known. Its
//      targets count from the bar after the fill, and a stop on the fill bar
//      counts. A limit is cancelled if the zone is invalidated, the RB expires,
//      or price reaches its TP2 before it fills. A CISD entry fills at the
//      trigger close, and its stop and targets count from the next bar.
//  A6. Expiry (default 16:00 NY): on the bar that ends 16:00 New York, unfilled
//      entries are cancelled, open trades close at that bar's close (realized R),
//      and every RB formed before it expires. With "Never", an RB still expires
//      4,500 chart bars after it formed, because TradingView can't draw further back.
//  A7. Stats count RBs whose three entries have all resolved. "→TP1" holds the
//      whole position to TP1 and "→TP2" to TP2, same stop, no breakeven.
//      A win is R > 0. Avg R is per filled trade.
//  A8. Premium/discount: a bearish RB's CE above the midnight open (the 18:00
//      open before midnight), a bullish RB's below it. Killzone is judged on the
//      RB candle's open time. Daily bias (PXH/PXL), from yesterday against the
//      day before: close above its high = bullish, close below its low =
//      bearish, took only its high and closed back inside = bearish, took only
//      its low and closed back inside = bullish; anything else = no bias. Or
//      the direction of yesterday's candle.
//  A9. Grade = how many hold: key level swept (key open / PDH-PDL / PWH-PWL),
//      killzone, premium/discount, daily bias, clean tip, and SMT when it is on
//      and its symbol has data.
//      With SMT (6 checks): A+ = 5-6, A = 4, B = 3, C = 0-2.
//      Without SMT (5 checks): A+ = 4-5, A = 3, B = 2, C = 0-1.
// A10. CISD level (R8) = open of the first candle in the unbroken run of candles
//      that closed toward the sweep and ran into the RB (the RB candle included
//      when it closed that way). With no such run, it is the RB candle's far
//      extreme. "CISD first" = that close happened before the zone's first touch,
//      within the displacement window.
// A11. SMT (R9): the RB candle and the same candle built from the SMT symbol's
//      chart bars are each compared with their own extreme over the previous N
//      RB candles. SMT holds when exactly one of the two broke it. The SMT symbol
//      is read on the chart timeframe, so it never repaints.
// A12. FVG first: within the displacement window and before the first touch,
//      a candle leaves a gap to the candle two before it, moving away from the
//      RB (bearish: its high below that candle's low). The RB candle can be the
//      first of the three.
// A13. CISD stop (R6): past the most extreme price between the tap and the
//      trigger, plus the buffer. Every stop is then moved out, if needed, to the
//      minimum distance from its entry. An RB's zone is still invalidated at its tip.
// =============================================================================

indicator("SaintTrades Rejection Block (ICT / Powell)", "ST RB", overlay=true, max_boxes_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500)

// ============================== TYPES ========================================
type Lvl
    float  price
    string name
    int    kind            // 0 = key open (two-sided), 1 = high-side liquidity, -1 = low-side liquidity
    int    tier            // 2 = key level, 1 = session, 0 = swing
    int    bornT           // earliest RB-candle open time that may use this level (A2)
    int    takenT          // first chart bar that traded through it (one-sided only)
    int    deadT           // replaced by a newer level of the same name at this time
    int    dayId
    int    bornBar
    line   ln
    label  lb

type Trade
    float entry
    float stop
    float tp1
    float tp2
    float risk
    bool  tapped    = false
    int   tapBar
    float ext
    int   extBar
    float cisd
    bool  filled    = false
    int   fillBar
    bool  cancelled = false
    bool  done1     = false
    bool  done2     = false
    float r1        = 0.0
    float r2        = 0.0

type RB
    bool   bull
    float  tip
    float  edge
    float  ce
    float  stop
    string names
    int    tier
    int    formT
    int    formBar
    int    trackFrom
    int    fillFrom
    float  cisdLvl
    int    age       = 0       // RB candles since it formed, up to the displacement window
    bool   disp      = false
    bool   dispFirst = false
    bool   fvg       = false
    bool   fvgFirst  = false
    float  fvgP1               // far extreme of the last candle, then of the one before it (A12)
    float  fvgP2
    bool   tapped    = false
    bool   invalid   = false
    bool   expired   = false
    bool   dropped   = false
    bool   resolved  = false
    bool   zoneDone  = false
    string resTxt    = ""      // the selected entry's result, shown on the label once it's done
    int    score
    string grade
    bool   fKey   = false
    bool   fKz    = false
    bool   fPd    = false
    bool   fBias  = false
    bool   fClean = false
    bool   fSmt   = false
    bool   fDir   = false
    Trade  t0
    Trade  t1
    Trade  t2
    box    bx
    line   ceLn
    label  tag
    label  fillMk
    line   lnE
    line   lnS
    line   lnT1
    line   lnT2
    label  lbE
    label  lbS
    label  lbT1
    label  lbT2

type State
    float atr

// =============================== INPUTS ======================================
G_RB  = "1 · Rejection block"
G_LV  = "2 · Levels the wick must run"
G_TR  = "3 · Entry, stop & targets"
G_FL  = "4 · Filters (off = measured only)"
G_VIS = "5 · Visuals"
G_ST  = "6 · Stats"

rbTfIn      = input.string("Chart", "RB timeframe", options=["Chart", "1m", "3m", "5m", "15m", "30m", "1H", "4H"], tooltip="The timeframe the rejection candle is read on. Powell marks RBs on the 5m and 15m. Use one at or above the chart timeframe that the chart timeframe divides into evenly, e.g. 5m or 15m RBs on a 1m chart.", group=G_RB)
zoneFrom    = input.string("Body edge", "Zone runs from", options=["Body edge", "Close", "Highest body in swing (ICT)"], tooltip="Body edge = the wick only: from the open or close nearest the wick to the tip. Close = from the close to the tip, which also takes in the body when the candle closed away from the wick. Highest body in swing (ICT) = when the candles just before it also wicked into this area, from the body nearest the tip among them to the tip, so the zone holds wicks only.", group=G_RB)
minWickPct  = input.float(40.0, "Rejecting wick ≥ % of candle range", minval=0, maxval=100, step=5, group=G_RB)
minWickBody = input.float(1.0, "Rejecting wick ≥ body ×", minval=0, step=0.25, group=G_RB)
minWickAtr  = input.float(0.25, "Rejecting wick ≥ ATR(14) ×", minval=0, step=0.05, tooltip="ATR of the RB timeframe. Ignores small wicks. 0 = off.", group=G_RB)
invMode     = input.string("Wick past tip (Powell)", "Invalidate when", options=["Wick past tip (Powell)", "Close past tip (ICT)"], group=G_RB)
dispWin     = input.int(6, "Displacement window (RB candles)", minval=1, maxval=50, tooltip="How many RB-timeframe candles after the RB may still close through its CISD level and count as displacement (R8).", group=G_RB)

useKO   = input.bool(true, "Powell key opens (New York time)", group=G_LV)
ko0000  = input.bool(true, "00:00", inline="ko1", group=G_LV)
ko0200  = input.bool(true, "02:00", inline="ko1", group=G_LV)
ko0830  = input.bool(true, "08:30", inline="ko1", group=G_LV)
ko0930  = input.bool(true, "09:30", inline="ko1", group=G_LV)
ko1000  = input.bool(true, "10:00", inline="ko2", group=G_LV)
ko1330  = input.bool(true, "13:30", inline="ko2", group=G_LV)
ko1800  = input.bool(true, "18:00", inline="ko2", group=G_LV)
usePD   = input.bool(true, "Previous day high / low", group=G_LV)
usePW   = input.bool(true, "Previous week high / low", group=G_LV)
useSes  = input.bool(true, "Session highs / lows: Asia 20-00, London 02-05, NY AM 09:30-12", group=G_LV)
useSw   = input.bool(true, "Swing highs / lows on the RB timeframe", group=G_LV)
swLen   = input.int(3, "Swing strength (candles each side)", minval=1, maxval=10, group=G_LV)
swKeep  = input.int(10, "Swing levels kept per side", minval=1, maxval=30, group=G_LV)
sweepTk = input.int(1, "Liquidity sweep: min ticks through", minval=0, maxval=100, tooltip="How far a wick must trade past a high or low to count as a sweep. Key opens only need a touch, as Powell draws them.", group=G_LV)
drawKO  = input.bool(true, "Draw today's key opens", group=G_LV)
drawLiq = input.bool(false, "Draw untaken liquidity levels", group=G_LV)

entrySel = input.string("CE limit", "Entry shown & alerted", options=["CE limit", "Body-edge limit", "CISD after tap"], tooltip="CE limit = limit at 50% of the wick. Body-edge limit = limit at the near edge of the zone. CISD after tap = market entry on the first close back through the open of the push into the zone. The stats table measures all three either way.", group=G_TR)
stopTk   = input.int(4, "Stop buffer past the tip (ticks)", minval=0, maxval=400, tooltip="4 ticks = 1 point on NQ/ES.", group=G_TR)
minStop  = input.int(20, "Minimum stop distance (ticks)", minval=0, maxval=4000, tooltip="A stop closer than this to its entry is moved out to this distance. Powell prefers about 5 NQ points (20 ticks) as the smallest stop. 0 = off.", group=G_TR)
cisdStop = input.string("Past post-tap extreme (Powell)", "CISD entry stop", options=["Past post-tap extreme (Powell)", "Past RB tip"], tooltip="Powell's entry trigger puts the stop past the high (shorts) or low (longs) made after price tapped the zone. Past RB tip uses the RB's own stop.", group=G_TR)
tp1R     = input.float(1.0, "TP1 (R)", minval=0.25, step=0.25, group=G_TR)
tp2Mode  = input.string("Fixed R", "TP2", options=["Fixed R", "Opposing liquidity"], tooltip="Opposing liquidity = the nearest untaken high (longs) or low (shorts) beyond TP1; key opens are not used. Falls back to the fixed R when there is none.", group=G_TR)
tp2R     = input.float(2.0, "TP2 (R)", minval=0.5, step=0.25, group=G_TR)
cisdWin  = input.int(12, "CISD entry: bars allowed after the tap", minval=1, maxval=300, tooltip="Chart bars after the first touch in which the CISD close must come, or that entry is cancelled.", group=G_TR)
expMode  = input.string("16:00 NY", "Expire / flatten", options=["16:00 NY", "Never"], tooltip="16:00 NY: on the bar that ends 16:00 New York, unfilled entries are cancelled, open trades close at that bar's close, and every RB formed before it expires. Never: RBs live until the tip is taken and trades run to stop or target.", group=G_TR)

minGrade = input.string("B", "Minimum grade to show", options=["A+", "A", "B", "C"], tooltip="Grade counts: key level swept (key open, PDH/PDL, PWH/PWL), killzone, premium/discount, daily bias, clean tip, and SMT when it is on. With SMT: A+ = 5-6, A = 4, B = 3, C = 0-2. Without: A+ = 4-5, A = 3, B = 2, C = 0-1.", group=G_FL)
reqKey   = input.bool(false, "Require a key level (key open / PDH-PDL / PWH-PWL)", group=G_FL)
reqKz    = input.bool(false, "Require killzone", group=G_FL)
kzLon    = input.bool(true, "London 02-05", inline="kz", group=G_FL)
kzAM     = input.bool(true, "NY AM 08:30-11", inline="kz", group=G_FL)
kzPM     = input.bool(true, "NY PM 13:30-16", inline="kz", group=G_FL)
reqPd    = input.bool(false, "Require premium (shorts) / discount (longs) vs midnight open", group=G_FL)
reqBias  = input.bool(false, "Require daily bias", group=G_FL)
biasMode = input.string("PXH/PXL (Powell)", "Daily bias from", options=["PXH/PXL (Powell)", "Previous day's candle"], tooltip="PXH/PXL: yesterday closed above the day before's high = bullish, below its low = bearish. Took only its high and closed back inside = bearish; took only its low and closed back inside = bullish. Anything else (inside day, both sides taken) = no bias. Previous day's candle = the direction yesterday closed.", group=G_FL)
useSmt   = input.bool(true, "SMT divergence with a correlated market", tooltip="Counted in the grade when on. SMT holds when the RB candle breaks the extreme of the last N RB candles and the other market's same candle doesn't, or the other way round.", group=G_FL)
smtSymIn = input.string("Auto", "SMT symbol", tooltip="Auto: ES for NQ/MNQ, NQ for ES/MES, ES for YM/MYM/RTY/M2K; anything else needs a symbol typed here, e.g. CME_MINI:ES1!.", group=G_FL)
smtLook  = input.int(12, "SMT lookback (RB candles)", minval=2, maxval=50, group=G_FL)
reqSmt   = input.bool(false, "Require SMT", group=G_FL)
reqDir   = input.bool(false, "Require the RB candle to close with the rejection (Powell)", tooltip="Bullish RB: the candle closes up. Bearish RB: it closes down.", group=G_FL)
reqClean = input.bool(false, "Require clean tip (no equal highs / lows)", group=G_FL)
eqTk     = input.int(4, "Equal high/low tolerance (ticks)", minval=0, maxval=400, group=G_FL)
eqLook   = input.int(20, "Equal high/low lookback (RB candles)", minval=2, maxval=50, group=G_FL)
reqDisp  = input.bool(false, "Require displacement (CISD) before the first touch", tooltip="RBs are drawn dashed until displacement prints. With this on, an RB touched before it displaced is removed and not traded.", group=G_FL)
reqFvg   = input.bool(false, "Require a displacement FVG before the first touch", tooltip="A fair value gap left by the move away from the RB, within the displacement window. With this on, an RB touched before one formed is removed and not traded.", group=G_FL)

colBull = input.color(#26a69a, "Bullish RB", inline="c1", group=G_VIS)
colBear = input.color(#ef5350, "Bearish RB", inline="c1", group=G_VIS)
colKO   = input.color(#b2b5be, "Key opens", inline="c2", group=G_VIS)
colLiq  = input.color(#787b86, "Liquidity", inline="c2", group=G_VIS)
colEnt  = input.color(#2962ff, "Entry", inline="c3", group=G_VIS)
colSl   = input.color(#ef5350, "Stop", inline="c3", group=G_VIS)
colTp   = input.color(#26a69a, "Targets", inline="c3", group=G_VIS)
showCE  = input.bool(true, "CE (50%) line", group=G_VIS)
lblMode = input.string("Compact", "RB labels", options=["Compact", "Full", "Off"], tooltip="Compact = direction, grade and ✓ once displaced, e.g. ▼ A ✓. Full also lists the levels the wick ran. Hover a label for the zone, CE, stop and filters.", group=G_VIS)
keepLbl = input.bool(true, "Keep labels on finished RBs", tooltip="On: a finished RB keeps its label, with the selected entry's result held to TP2 (e.g. ▼ B · +2.0R, -1.0R, no fill). Off: the label goes when the zone ends; the dotted box stays.", group=G_VIS)
maxKeep = input.int(8, "RBs kept on the chart", minval=1, maxval=100, tooltip="Older drawings are deleted first. RBs still in play keep being tracked for the stats after their drawings go.", group=G_VIS)
lvlN    = input.int(1, "Entry / stop / TP lines for the newest N live RBs", minval=0, maxval=5, group=G_VIS)

tblMode   = input.string("Compact", "Stats table", options=["Compact", "Full", "Off"], tooltip="Compact = the three entries compared. Full adds the filter lab and the grade rows.", group=G_ST)
statsPos  = input.string("Top Right", "Table position", options=["Top Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Right", "Bottom Left", "Middle Right"], group=G_ST)

// ============================= CONSTANTS =====================================
NY   = "America/New_York"
TICK = syminfo.mintick

rbTf = switch rbTfIn
    "1m"  => "1"
    "3m"  => "3"
    "5m"  => "5"
    "15m" => "15"
    "30m" => "30"
    "1H"  => "60"
    "4H"  => "240"
    => timeframe.period
useAgg = rbTf != timeframe.period
if useAgg and timeframe.in_seconds(rbTf) < timeframe.in_seconds()
    runtime.error("The RB timeframe must be at or above the chart timeframe.")

invWick = invMode == "Wick past tip (Powell)"
zoneSwing = zoneFrom == "Highest body in swing (ICT)"
powellStop = cisdStop == "Past post-tap extreme (Powell)"
pxhBias = biasMode == "PXH/PXL (Powell)"

// R9: the SMT partner. Index futures pair with ES, ES pairs with NQ.
smtAuto = switch syminfo.root
    "NQ"  => "CME_MINI:ES1!"
    "MNQ" => "CME_MINI:ES1!"
    "ES"  => "CME_MINI:NQ1!"
    "MES" => "CME_MINI:NQ1!"
    "YM"  => "CME_MINI:ES1!"
    "MYM" => "CME_MINI:ES1!"
    "RTY" => "CME_MINI:ES1!"
    "M2K" => "CME_MINI:ES1!"
    => ""
smtSym = not useSmt ? "" : smtSymIn == "Auto" ? smtAuto : str.trim(smtSymIn)
smtOn  = smtSym != "" and smtSym != syminfo.tickerid and smtSym != syminfo.ticker
showStats = tblMode != "Off"
fullTbl   = tblMode == "Full"
// TradingView refuses drawings anchored ~10,000 bars back; RBs this old expire (A6)
MAX_AGE = 4500
selIdx  = entrySel == "CE limit" ? 0 : entrySel == "Body-edge limit" ? 1 : 2

// ============================== STATE ========================================
var State      S    = State.new()
var array<Lvl> lvls = array.new<Lvl>()
var array<RB>  rbs  = array.new<RB>()

// closed RB-timeframe candles, oldest first
var array<float> hO = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hH = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hL = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hC = array.new<float>()
// the same candles built from the SMT symbol's bars (A11)
var array<float> sHH = array.new<float>()
var array<float> sHL = array.new<float>()

// stats per entry method (0 CE, 1 edge, 2 CISD) and filter-lab rows
var array<int>   eFill = array.new<int>(3, 0)
var array<float> eS1   = array.new<float>(3, 0.0)
var array<int>   eW1   = array.new<int>(3, 0)
var array<float> eS2   = array.new<float>(3, 0.0)
var array<int>   eW2   = array.new<int>(3, 0)
LAB_N = 14
var array<int>   lN  = array.new<int>(LAB_N, 0)
var array<float> lS1 = array.new<float>(LAB_N, 0.0)
var array<int>   lW1 = array.new<int>(LAB_N, 0)
var array<float> lS2 = array.new<float>(LAB_N, 0.0)
var array<int>   lW2 = array.new<int>(LAB_N, 0)
var int setups = 0

// day / week / session context
var float dO          = na
var float dH          = na
var float dL          = na
var bool  prevDayBull = false
var bool  haveBias    = false
var float ppH         = na     // the day before yesterday's high / low (PXH/PXL, A8)
var float ppL         = na
var int   pxBias      = 0      // 1 bullish, -1 bearish, 0 none
var float wH          = na
var float wL          = na
var float mOpen       = na
var int   mOpenDay    = -1
var int   koDay       = 0      // New York trading day for key opens and P/D, rolls at 18:00 (A3)
var float koOpen      = na     // the 18:00 open
var bool  sawEve      = false  // the symbol trades at/after 18:00 NY
var float asH = na
var float asL = na
var float lnH = na
var float lnL = na
var float nyH = na
var float nyL = na
var bool  inAs = false
var bool  inLn = false
var bool  inNy = false

// chart-bar runs for the CISD trigger: open of the first bar of the current up/down-close run
var float upRun = na
var float dnRun = na

// RB-timeframe candle being built
var float aO    = na
var float aH    = na
var float aL    = na
var float aC    = na
var int   aT    = na
var int   aBar  = na
var bool  aDone = true
var float sAH   = na     // the SMT symbol's high / low over the same candle
var float sAL   = na
var bool  smtSeen = false

// ============================== HELPERS ======================================
nyMin(int t) =>
    hour(t, NY) * 60 + minute(t, NY)

// ---- per-bar context. Called every bar so their state stays consistent; used on confirmed bars only.
bool tfChg     = timeframe.change(rbTf)
bool newRbBar  = not useAgg or tfChg
int  rbCloseT  = time_close(rbTf)
bool lastRbBar = not useAgg or (not na(rbCloseT) and time_close == rbCloseT)
bool newDay    = timeframe.change("D")
bool newWeek   = timeframe.change("W")
int  mNow      = nyMin(time)
int  mCls      = na(time_close) ? na : nyMin(time_close)
int  nyDom     = dayofmonth(time, NY)
bool newNyDate = na(nyDom[1]) or nyDom != nyDom[1]
int  mPrv      = mNow[1]
bool cross18   = not na(mPrv) and mNow >= 1080 and (mPrv < 1080 or time - time[1] >= 43200000)
bool flatNow   = expMode == "16:00 NY" and not na(mCls) and mNow < 960 and mCls >= 960
// A11: the SMT symbol on the chart timeframe (na when SMT is off or the symbol has no data)
[smtHi, smtLo] = request.security(smtOn ? smtSym : syminfo.tickerid, timeframe.period, [high, low], ignore_invalid_symbol=true)
float sHi = smtOn ? smtHi : na
float sLo = smtOn ? smtLo : na

// A9: 6 checks once the SMT symbol has delivered data, else 5
gradeOf(int s) =>
    int n = smtOn and smtSeen ? 6 : 5
    s >= n - 1 ? "A+" : s == n - 2 ? "A" : s == n - 3 ? "B" : "C"

// A8: today's daily bias, 1 bullish, -1 bearish, 0 none
dayBias() =>
    pxhBias ? pxBias : haveBias ? (prevDayBull ? 1 : -1) : 0

// R7/A13: move a stop out to the minimum distance from its entry
widen(bool bull, float e, float s) =>
    float d = math.max(bull ? e - s : s - e, minStop * TICK)
    bull ? e - d : e + d

gRank(string g) =>
    g == "A+" ? 3 : g == "A" ? 2 : g == "B" ? 1 : 0

f_pct(int a, int b) =>
    b > 0 ? str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * a / b)) + "%" : "-"

// average R and win rate, e.g. "+0.42R · 55%"
fR(float sum, int wins, int n) =>
    n > 0 ? (sum / n >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(sum / n, "0.00") + "R · " + str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * wins / n)) + "%" : "-"

isDone(Trade t) =>
    t.cancelled or (t.filled and t.done1 and t.done2)

selTrade(RB r) =>
    selIdx == 0 ? r.t0 : selIdx == 1 ? r.t1 : r.t2

// A level is born (R2). Key opens are dotted, liquidity dashed.
addLvl(float p, string n, int k, int tier, int bt, int d) =>
    Lvl lv = Lvl.new(price=p, name=n, kind=k, tier=tier, bornT=bt, dayId=d, bornBar=bar_index)
    if k == 0 ? drawKO : drawLiq
        color c = k == 0 ? colKO : colLiq
        lv.ln := line.new(bar_index, p, bar_index + 1, p, color=color.new(c, 30), style=k == 0 ? line.style_dotted : line.style_dashed, width=1)
        lv.lb := label.new(bar_index, p, n, color=color.new(color.black, 100), style=label.style_label_lower_left, textcolor=c, size=size.tiny)
    array.push(lvls, lv)
    true

dropLvl(int i) =>
    Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
    line.delete(lv.ln)
    label.delete(lv.lb)
    array.remove(lvls, i)
    true

// a new session/day/week level replaces the previous one of the same name. The old
// one stays usable for a candle that opened before now and is removed after this bar.
killName(string n) =>
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if lv.name == n and na(lv.deadT)
                lv.deadT := time
    true

// keep only the newest swKeep swing levels per side
trimSwings(int k) =>
    int cnt = 0
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = array.size(lvls) - 1 to 0
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if lv.tier == 0 and lv.kind == k
                cnt += 1
                if cnt > swKeep
                    dropLvl(i)
    true

// R7: TP2 at a fixed R, or at the nearest untaken opposing liquidity beyond TP1
tp2For(bool bull, float e, float rk) =>
    float res = bull ? e + tp2R * rk : e - tp2R * rk
    if tp2Mode == "Opposing liquidity" and array.size(lvls) > 0
        float t1 = bull ? e + tp1R * rk : e - tp1R * rk
        float best = na
        for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if na(lv.takenT) and na(lv.deadT) and (bull ? lv.kind == 1 and lv.price > t1 : lv.kind == -1 and lv.price < t1)
                if na(best) or (bull ? lv.price < best : lv.price > best)
                    best := lv.price
        if not na(best)
            res := best
    res

// A5: one bar of a resting limit. Returns true when it fills on this bar.
stepLimit(Trade t, bool bull, bool canFill, bool deadBefore, bool deadNow) =>
    bool filledNow = false
    if not t.filled and not t.cancelled
        if deadBefore
            t.cancelled := true
        else if canFill and (bull ? low <= t.entry : high >= t.entry)
            t.filled := true
            t.fillBar := bar_index
            filledNow := true
        else if deadNow or (bull ? high >= t.tp2 : low <= t.tp2)
            t.cancelled := true
    filledNow

// R6: CISD after tap. The first touch arms it; each new extreme resets the CISD
// level to the open of the run that made it; the entry is the first close back
// through that level. Returns true when it fills on this bar.
stepCisd(Trade t, RB r, bool canFill, bool deadBefore, bool deadNow, float cisdHere, bool flat) =>
    bool filledNow = false
    bool bull = r.bull
    Trade ceT = r.t0
    if not t.filled and not t.cancelled
        if deadBefore
            t.cancelled := true
        else if not t.tapped
            if canFill and (bull ? low <= r.edge : high >= r.edge)
                t.tapped := true
                t.tapBar := bar_index
                t.ext := bull ? low : high
                t.extBar := bar_index
                t.cisd := cisdHere
            else if deadNow or (bull ? high >= ceT.tp2 : low <= ceT.tp2)
                t.cancelled := true
        else
            if bull ? low <= t.ext : high >= t.ext
                t.ext := bull ? low : high
                t.extBar := bar_index
                t.cisd := cisdHere
            else if not flat and not deadNow and not na(t.cisd) and bar_index > t.extBar and (bull ? close > t.cisd : close < t.cisd)
                // A13: Powell's stop goes past the extreme made since the tap
                float sBase = powellStop ? (bull ? t.ext - stopTk * TICK : t.ext + stopTk * TICK) : r.stop
                float sC = widen(bull, close, sBase)
                float rk = bull ? close - sC : sC - close
                if rk > 0 and (bull ? close > sBase : close < sBase)
                    t.stop := sC
                    t.entry := close
                    t.risk := rk
                    t.tp1 := bull ? close + tp1R * rk : close - tp1R * rk
                    t.tp2 := tp2For(bull, close, rk)
                    t.filled := true
                    t.fillBar := bar_index
                    filledNow := true
            if not t.filled and (deadNow or bar_index - t.tapBar >= cisdWin)
                t.cancelled := true
    filledNow

// A5/A6: one bar of an open position. Stop first (conservative); targets from the
// bar after the fill. A limit can stop out on its fill bar; a CISD (market) entry
// is taken at the close, so its first bar is the next one.
stepOpen(Trade t, bool bull, bool mkt, bool flat) =>
    if t.filled and not (t.done1 and t.done2)
        bool after = bar_index > t.fillBar
        bool stopHit = (after or not mkt) and (bull ? low <= t.stop : high >= t.stop)
        if stopHit
            if not t.done1
                t.r1 := -1.0
                t.done1 := true
            if not t.done2
                t.r2 := -1.0
                t.done2 := true
        else if after
            if not t.done1 and (bull ? high >= t.tp1 : low <= t.tp1)
                t.r1 := math.abs(t.tp1 - t.entry) / t.risk
                t.done1 := true
            if not t.done2 and (bull ? high >= t.tp2 : low <= t.tp2)
                t.r2 := math.abs(t.tp2 - t.entry) / t.risk
                t.done2 := true
        if flat and not (t.done1 and t.done2)
            float rNow = (bull ? close - t.entry : t.entry - close) / t.risk
            if not t.done1
                t.r1 := rNow
                t.done1 := true
            if not t.done2
                t.r2 := rNow
                t.done2 := true
    true

// ---- drawing ----
upLine(line ln, int x1, float y, color c) =>
    line res = ln
    if na(y)
        line.delete(ln)
        res := na
    else if na(ln)
        res := line.new(x1, y, bar_index, y, color=c, style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
    else
        line.set_xy1(ln, x1, y)
        line.set_xy2(ln, bar_index, y)
    res

upLab(label lb, float y, color c, string txt) =>
    label res = lb
    if na(y)
        label.delete(lb)
        res := na
    else if na(lb)
        res := label.new(bar_index, y, txt, color=color.new(color.black, 100), style=label.style_label_left, textcolor=c, size=size.tiny)
    else
        label.set_xy(lb, bar_index, y)
        label.set_text(lb, txt)
    res

clearTrade(RB r) =>
    line.delete(r.lnE)
    line.delete(r.lnS)
    line.delete(r.lnT1)
    line.delete(r.lnT2)
    label.delete(r.lbE)
    label.delete(r.lbS)
    label.delete(r.lbT1)
    label.delete(r.lbT2)
    r.lnE := na
    r.lnS := na
    r.lnT1 := na
    r.lnT2 := na
    r.lbE := na
    r.lbS := na
    r.lbT1 := na
    r.lbT2 := na
    true

// entry / stop / TP lines for the selected entry of a live RB
drawTrade(RB r) =>
    Trade t = selTrade(r)
    bool waitC = selIdx == 2 and not t.filled
    float yE  = waitC ? r.edge : t.entry
    float yT1 = waitC ? na : t.tp1
    float yT2 = waitC ? na : t.tp2
    string eTxt = waitC ? "Tap → wait for CISD" : "Entry " + str.tostring(yE, format.mintick)
    int x1 = math.max(r.formBar, bar_index - MAX_AGE)
    r.lnE := upLine(r.lnE, x1, yE, colEnt)
    r.lbE := upLab(r.lbE, yE, colEnt, eTxt)
    float yS = waitC or na(t.stop) ? r.stop : t.stop
    r.lnS := upLine(r.lnS, x1, yS, colSl)
    r.lbS := upLab(r.lbS, yS, colSl, "SL " + str.tostring(yS, format.mintick))
    r.lnT1 := upLine(r.lnT1, x1, yT1, colTp)
    r.lbT1 := upLab(r.lbT1, yT1, colTp, waitC ? "" : "TP1 " + str.tostring(yT1, format.mintick))
    r.lnT2 := upLine(r.lnT2, x1, yT2, colTp)
    r.lbT2 := upLab(r.lbT2, yT2, colTp, waitC ? "" : "TP2 " + str.tostring(yT2, format.mintick))
    true

deleteDrawings(RB r) =>
    box.delete(r.bx)
    line.delete(r.ceLn)
    label.delete(r.tag)
    label.delete(r.fillMk)
    r.bx := na
    r.ceLn := na
    r.tag := na
    r.fillMk := na
    clearTrade(r)
    true

yes(bool b) =>
    b ? "✓" : "✗"

tagText(RB r) =>
    string t = (r.bull ? "▲ " : "▼ ") + r.grade + (r.disp ? " ✓" : "")
    t := lblMode == "Full" ? t + " · " + r.names : t
    r.resTxt == "" ? t : t + " · " + r.resTxt

// whether an RB keeps its label once its zone has ended
keepTag(RB r) =>
    keepLbl

tagTip(RB r) =>
    (r.bull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " rejection block, grade " + r.grade + "\nRan: " + r.names + "\nZone: " + str.tostring(math.min(r.tip, r.edge), format.mintick) + " – " + str.tostring(math.max(r.tip, r.edge), format.mintick) + "\nCE: " + str.tostring(r.ce, format.mintick) + "   Stop: " + str.tostring(r.stop, format.mintick) + "\nKey level " + yes(r.fKey) + " · Killzone " + yes(r.fKz) + " · P/D " + yes(r.fPd) + " · Bias " + yes(r.fBias) + " · Clean tip " + yes(r.fClean) + (smtOn ? " · SMT " + yes(r.fSmt) : "") + "\nClosed with the rejection " + yes(r.fDir) + "\nCISD: " + (r.disp ? "printed" : "waiting") + " at " + str.tostring(r.cisdLvl, format.mintick) + " · FVG: " + (r.fvg ? "printed" : "none yet")

drawNew(RB r) =>
    color c = r.bull ? colBull : colBear
    r.bx := box.new(left=r.formBar, top=math.max(r.tip, r.edge), right=bar_index, bottom=math.min(r.tip, r.edge), border_color=color.new(c, 30), border_style=r.disp ? line.style_solid : line.style_dashed, bgcolor=color.new(c, 85))
    if showCE
        r.ceLn := line.new(r.formBar, r.ce, bar_index, r.ce, color=color.new(c, 20), style=line.style_dotted, width=1)
    if lblMode != "Off"
        r.tag := label.new(r.formBar, r.tip, tagText(r), color=color.new(color.black, 100), style=r.bull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, textcolor=c, size=size.tiny, tooltip=tagTip(r))
    true

// the zone has stopped being live: freeze and dim its drawings
endZone(RB r) =>
    r.zoneDone := true
    color c = r.bull ? colBull : colBear
    if not keepTag(r)
        label.delete(r.tag)
        r.tag := na
    if not na(r.tag)
        label.set_textcolor(r.tag, color.new(c, 25))
    if not na(r.bx)
        box.set_right(r.bx, bar_index)
        box.set_bgcolor(r.bx, color.new(c, 90))
        box.set_border_color(r.bx, color.new(c, 40))
        box.set_border_style(r.bx, line.style_dotted)
    if not na(r.ceLn)
        line.set_x2(r.ceLn, bar_index)
        line.set_color(r.ceLn, color.new(c, 50))
    true

// A7: add a resolved RB to the stats
countRB(RB r) =>
    for m = 0 to 2
        Trade t = m == 0 ? r.t0 : m == 1 ? r.t1 : r.t2
        if t.filled
            array.set(eFill, m, array.get(eFill, m) + 1)
            array.set(eS1, m, array.get(eS1, m) + t.r1)
            array.set(eW1, m, array.get(eW1, m) + (t.r1 > 0 ? 1 : 0))
            array.set(eS2, m, array.get(eS2, m) + t.r2)
            array.set(eW2, m, array.get(eW2, m) + (t.r2 > 0 ? 1 : 0))
    Trade ts = selTrade(r)
    if ts.filled
        for k = 0 to LAB_N - 1
            bool inRow = switch k
                0 => true
                1 => r.fKey
                2 => r.fKz
                3 => r.fPd
                4 => r.fBias
                5 => r.fClean
                6 => r.fSmt
                7 => r.fDir
                8 => r.dispFirst
                9 => r.fvgFirst
                10 => r.grade == "A+"
                11 => r.grade == "A"
                12 => r.grade == "B"
                => r.grade == "C"
            if inRow
                array.set(lN, k, array.get(lN, k) + 1)
                array.set(lS1, k, array.get(lS1, k) + ts.r1)
                array.set(lW1, k, array.get(lW1, k) + (ts.r1 > 0 ? 1 : 0))
                array.set(lS2, k, array.get(lS2, k) + ts.r2)
                array.set(lW2, k, array.get(lW2, k) + (ts.r2 > 0 ? 1 : 0))
    true

// Finalize one closed RB-timeframe candle: displacement for live RBs (R8), then
// look for a new RB (R1-R4) against the levels as they stood before it (A2),
// then store the candle, confirm swing points and drop spent liquidity.
// late = finalized on the first bar of the next candle (A1).
// sh / sl = the SMT symbol's high / low over the same candle (A11).
// Returns [new RB or na, an RB that just displaced before its first touch or na].
finalize(float o, float h, float l, float c, int cT, int b0, bool late, float sh, float sl) =>
    RB armed = na
    if array.size(rbs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(rbs) - 1
            RB r = array.get(rbs, i)
            if not r.resolved and not r.zoneDone and r.formT < cT and r.age < dispWin
                r.age += 1
                bool changed = false
                if not r.disp and (r.bull ? c > r.cisdLvl : c < r.cisdLvl)
                    r.disp := true
                    r.dispFirst := not r.tapped
                    changed := true
                    if not na(r.bx)
                        box.set_border_style(r.bx, line.style_solid)
                    if r.dispFirst
                        armed := r
                // A12: a gap between this candle and the one two before it
                if not r.fvg and not na(r.fvgP2) and (r.bull ? l > r.fvgP2 : h < r.fvgP2)
                    r.fvg := true
                    r.fvgFirst := not r.tapped
                    changed := true
                r.fvgP2 := r.fvgP1
                r.fvgP1 := r.bull ? h : l
                if changed and not na(r.tag)
                    label.set_text(r.tag, tagText(r))
                    label.set_tooltip(r.tag, tagTip(r))

    float bodyTop = math.max(o, c)
    float bodyBot = math.min(o, c)
    float rng  = h - l
    float upW  = h - bodyTop
    float dnW  = bodyBot - l
    float body = bodyTop - bodyBot
    float atrV = S.atr
    bool bearShape = rng > 0 and upW >= minWickPct / 100.0 * rng and upW >= minWickBody * body and upW > dnW and (na(atrV) or minWickAtr <= 0 or upW >= minWickAtr * atrV)
    bool bullShape = rng > 0 and dnW >= minWickPct / 100.0 * rng and dnW >= minWickBody * body and dnW > upW and (na(atrV) or minWickAtr <= 0 or dnW >= minWickAtr * atrV)
    RB rbNew = na
    if (bearShape or bullShape) and array.size(lvls) > 0
        bool bull = bullShape
        array<string> nm2 = array.new<string>()
        array<string> nm1 = array.new<string>()
        array<string> nm0 = array.new<string>()
        int bestTier = -1
        for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if lv.bornT <= cT and (na(lv.deadT) or cT < lv.deadT)
                bool untaken = na(lv.takenT) or lv.takenT >= cT
                bool hit = false
                if lv.kind == 0
                    hit := bull ? l <= lv.price and bodyBot > lv.price : h >= lv.price and bodyTop < lv.price
                else if bull and lv.kind == -1 and untaken
                    hit := l <= lv.price - sweepTk * TICK and bodyBot > lv.price
                else if not bull and lv.kind == 1 and untaken
                    hit := h >= lv.price + sweepTk * TICK and bodyTop < lv.price
                if hit
                    array.push(lv.tier == 2 ? nm2 : lv.tier == 1 ? nm1 : nm0, lv.name)
                    bestTier := math.max(bestTier, lv.tier)
        if bestTier >= 0
            // label names, key levels first, at most three
            array<string> nmAll = array.concat(array.concat(nm2, nm1), nm0)
            string names = array.join(array.slice(nmAll, 0, math.min(3, array.size(nmAll))), "+") + (array.size(nmAll) > 3 ? "+" + str.tostring(array.size(nmAll) - 3) : "")
            float tip  = bull ? l : h
            float edge = zoneFrom == "Close" ? c : bull ? bodyBot : bodyTop
            // R3/A4 ICT option: the body nearest the tip among the candles just before
            // it whose wicks reached this candle's body without going past its tip
            if zoneSwing
                int jc = array.size(hO) - 1
                int nc = 0
                while jc >= 0 and nc < 5
                    float xc = bull ? array.get(hL, jc) : array.get(hH, jc)
                    if bull ? xc > bodyBot or xc < tip : xc < bodyTop or xc > tip
                        break
                    float bc = bull ? math.min(array.get(hO, jc), array.get(hC, jc)) : math.max(array.get(hO, jc), array.get(hC, jc))
                    if bull ? bc < edge and bc > tip : bc > edge and bc < tip
                        edge := bc
                    jc -= 1
                    nc += 1
            float ce   = (tip + edge) / 2
            // A4: a wick inside a live RB of the same direction is a retest of it
            bool dup = false
            if array.size(rbs) > 0
                for i = 0 to array.size(rbs) - 1
                    RB q = array.get(rbs, i)
                    if q.bull == bull and not q.zoneDone and not q.resolved and not q.dropped
                        if bull ? tip >= q.tip and tip <= q.edge : tip <= q.tip and tip >= q.edge
                            dup := true
            // A8/A9 filters
            bool fKey = bestTier == 2
            int  mO   = nyMin(cT)
            bool fKz  = (kzLon and mO >= 120 and mO < 300) or (kzAM and mO >= 510 and mO < 660) or (kzPM and mO >= 810 and mO < 960)
            float pdRef = mOpenDay == koDay ? mOpen : nz(koOpen, dO)
            bool fPd   = not na(pdRef) and (bull ? ce < pdRef : ce > pdRef)
            int  bias  = dayBias()
            bool fBias = bull ? bias == 1 : bias == -1
            bool fDir  = bull ? c > o : c < o
            bool fClean = true
            int n = array.size(hH)
            if n > 0
                int j0 = math.max(0, n - eqLook)
                for j = j0 to n - 1
                    float x = bull ? array.get(hL, j) : array.get(hH, j)
                    if math.abs(x - tip) <= eqTk * TICK
                        fClean := false
            // A11: SMT = exactly one of the two markets broke its own extreme of the last smtLook candles
            bool fSmt = false
            if smtOn and not na(sh) and not na(sl) and n >= smtLook
                float mRef = na
                float sRef = na
                for j = n - smtLook to n - 1
                    float mj = bull ? array.get(hL, j) : array.get(hH, j)
                    float sj = bull ? array.get(sHL, j) : array.get(sHH, j)
                    mRef := na(mRef) ? mj : bull ? math.min(mRef, mj) : math.max(mRef, mj)
                    if not na(sj)
                        sRef := na(sRef) ? sj : bull ? math.min(sRef, sj) : math.max(sRef, sj)
                if not na(sRef)
                    bool mBrk = bull ? l < mRef : h > mRef
                    bool sBrk = bull ? sl < sRef : sh > sRef
                    fSmt := mBrk != sBrk
            int score = (fKey ? 1 : 0) + (fKz ? 1 : 0) + (fPd ? 1 : 0) + (fBias ? 1 : 0) + (fClean ? 1 : 0) + (smtOn and fSmt ? 1 : 0)
            string grade = gradeOf(score)
            bool show = not flatNow and not dup and gRank(grade) >= gRank(minGrade) and (not reqKey or fKey) and (not reqKz or fKz) and (not reqPd or fPd) and (not reqBias or fBias) and (not reqClean or fClean) and (not reqSmt or fSmt) and (not reqDir or fDir)
            // A10: CISD level = open of the run of candles that pushed into the sweep
            float runOpen = na
            if bull ? c < o : c > o
                runOpen := o
            int jj = array.size(hO) - 1
            int steps = 0
            while jj >= 0 and steps < 10
                float oj = array.get(hO, jj)
                float cj = array.get(hC, jj)
                if bull ? cj < oj : cj > oj
                    runOpen := oj
                    jj -= 1
                    steps += 1
                else
                    break
            float cisdLvl = na(runOpen) ? (bull ? h : l) : runOpen
            bool dispNow = bull ? c > cisdLvl : c < cisdLvl
            // A1: a late candle is dropped if this bar already took its tip
            bool tapNow = false
            if show and late
                bool invNow = invWick ? (bull ? low < tip : high > tip) : (bull ? close < tip : close > tip)
                tapNow := bull ? low <= edge : high >= edge
                // an FVG needs two more candles, so it can't come before this touch
                if invNow or (tapNow and reqDisp and not dispNow) or (tapNow and reqFvg)
                    show := false
            if show
                float stop = bull ? tip - stopTk * TICK : tip + stopTk * TICK
                float sA  = widen(bull, ce, stop)
                float sB  = widen(bull, edge, stop)
                float rkA = math.abs(sA - ce)
                float rkB = math.abs(sB - edge)
                Trade tA = Trade.new(entry=ce, stop=sA, risk=rkA, tp1=bull ? ce + tp1R * rkA : ce - tp1R * rkA, tp2=tp2For(bull, ce, rkA))
                Trade tB = Trade.new(entry=edge, stop=sB, risk=rkB, tp1=bull ? edge + tp1R * rkB : edge - tp1R * rkB, tp2=tp2For(bull, edge, rkB))
                Trade tC = Trade.new(stop=stop)
                rbNew := RB.new(bull=bull, tip=tip, edge=edge, ce=ce, stop=stop, names=names, tier=bestTier, formT=cT, formBar=b0, trackFrom=bar_index + 1, fillFrom=bar_index + 1, cisdLvl=cisdLvl, disp=dispNow, dispFirst=dispNow, tapped=tapNow, fvgP1=bull ? h : l, score=score, grade=grade, fKey=fKey, fKz=fKz, fPd=fPd, fBias=fBias, fClean=fClean, fSmt=fSmt, fDir=fDir, t0=tA, t1=tB, t2=tC)

    // store the candle and update ATR(14) of the RB timeframe
    int nh = array.size(hC)
    float prevC = nh > 0 ? array.get(hC, nh - 1) : na
    float tr = na(prevC) ? h - l : math.max(h, prevC) - math.min(l, prevC)
    S.atr := na(S.atr) ? tr : S.atr + (tr - S.atr) / 14.0
    array.push(hO, o)
    array.push(hH, h)
    array.push(hL, l)
    array.push(hC, c)
    array.push(sHH, sh)
    array.push(sHL, sl)
    if array.size(hO) > 60
        array.shift(hO)
        array.shift(hH)
        array.shift(hL)
        array.shift(hC)
        array.shift(sHH)
        array.shift(sHL)

    // swing points confirmed by this candle (live from its close, A2)
    if useSw
        int ns = array.size(hH)
        if ns >= 2 * swLen + 1
            int cI = ns - 1 - swLen
            float ph = array.get(hH, cI)
            float pl = array.get(hL, cI)
            bool isPH = true
            bool isPL = true
            for k = cI - swLen to cI + swLen
                if k != cI
                    if array.get(hH, k) >= ph
                        isPH := false
                    if array.get(hL, k) <= pl
                        isPL := false
            int bt = late ? time : time_close
            if isPH
                addLvl(ph, "Swing H", 1, 0, bt, koDay)
                trimSwings(1)
            if isPL
                addLvl(pl, "Swing L", -1, 0, bt, koDay)
                trimSwings(-1)

    // one-sided liquidity traded through by this candle (or before it) is spent
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = array.size(lvls) - 1 to 0
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if lv.kind != 0 and not na(lv.takenT) and (not late or lv.takenT < time)
                dropLvl(i)
    [rbNew, armed]

// ============================== ENGINE =======================================
bool aNewBull = false
bool aNewBear = false
bool aArmed   = false
bool aFill    = false
bool aInval   = false

if barstate.isconfirmed
    // ---- chart-bar runs for the CISD trigger (R6)
    float prevUp = upRun
    float prevDn = dnRun
    if close > open
        upRun := na(upRun) ? open : upRun
        dnRun := na
    else if close < open
        dnRun := na(dnRun) ? open : dnRun
        upRun := na
    else
        upRun := na
        dnRun := na
    float cisdBear = close > open ? upRun : na(prevUp) ? open : prevUp
    float cisdBull = close < open ? dnRun : na(prevDn) ? open : prevDn

    // ---- level births (R2)
    if newDay
        if not na(dO)
            prevDayBull := close[1] > dO
            haveBias := true
            // A8 PXH/PXL: yesterday (dH, dL, its close) against the day before (ppH, ppL)
            if not na(ppH)
                float yc = close[1]
                pxBias := yc > ppH ? 1 : yc < ppL ? -1 : dH > ppH and dL >= ppL ? -1 : dL < ppL and dH <= ppH ? 1 : 0
            ppH := dH
            ppL := dL
        if usePD and not na(dH)
            killName("PDH")
            killName("PDL")
            addLvl(dH, "PDH", 1, 2, time, koDay)
            addLvl(dL, "PDL", -1, 2, time, koDay)
        dO := open
        dH := high
        dL := low
    else
        if na(dO)
            dO := open
        dH := na(dH) ? high : math.max(dH, high)
        dL := na(dL) ? low : math.min(dL, low)
    if newWeek
        if usePW and not na(wH)
            killName("PWH")
            killName("PWL")
            addLvl(wH, "PWH", 1, 2, time, koDay)
            addLvl(wL, "PWL", -1, 2, time, koDay)
        wH := high
        wL := low
    else
        wH := na(wH) ? high : math.max(wH, high)
        wL := na(wL) ? low : math.min(wL, low)
    if mNow >= 1080
        sawEve := true
    if sawEve ? cross18 : newDay
        koDay += 1
        koOpen := open
    if newNyDate
        mOpen := open
        mOpenDay := koDay
    if useKO
        string koName = mNow == 0 and ko0000 ? "00:00" : mNow == 120 and ko0200 ? "02:00" : mNow == 510 and ko0830 ? "08:30" : mNow == 570 and ko0930 ? "09:30" : mNow == 600 and ko1000 ? "10:00" : mNow == 810 and ko1330 ? "13:30" : mNow == 1080 and ko1800 ? "18:00" : ""
        if koName != ""
            addLvl(open, koName, 0, 2, time + 1, koDay)
    if useSes
        bool nAs = mNow >= 1200
        bool nLn = mNow >= 120 and mNow < 300
        bool nNy = mNow >= 570 and mNow < 720
        if nAs
            asH := inAs ? math.max(asH, high) : high
            asL := inAs ? math.min(asL, low) : low
        else if inAs
            killName("Asia H")
            killName("Asia L")
            addLvl(asH, "Asia H", 1, 1, time, koDay)
            addLvl(asL, "Asia L", -1, 1, time, koDay)
        if nLn
            lnH := inLn ? math.max(lnH, high) : high
            lnL := inLn ? math.min(lnL, low) : low
        else if inLn
            killName("London H")
            killName("London L")
            addLvl(lnH, "London H", 1, 1, time, koDay)
            addLvl(lnL, "London L", -1, 1, time, koDay)
        if nNy
            nyH := inNy ? math.max(nyH, high) : high
            nyL := inNy ? math.min(nyL, low) : low
        else if inNy
            killName("NY AM H")
            killName("NY AM L")
            addLvl(nyH, "NY AM H", 1, 1, time, koDay)
            addLvl(nyL, "NY AM L", -1, 1, time, koDay)
        inAs := nAs
        inLn := nLn
        inNy := nNy

    // ---- one-sided liquidity traded through on this bar (A2)
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if lv.kind != 0 and na(lv.takenT) and time >= lv.bornT
                if lv.kind == 1 ? high >= lv.price + sweepTk * TICK : low <= lv.price - sweepTk * TICK
                    lv.takenT := time

    // ---- track every RB already on the chart through this bar (R5, R6, A5, A6)
    if array.size(rbs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(rbs) - 1
            RB r = array.get(rbs, i)
            if not r.resolved and bar_index >= r.trackFrom
                bool deadBefore = r.zoneDone
                bool deadNow = false
                bool invNow = false
                Trade tsI = selTrade(r)
                bool selLive = not tsI.filled and not tsI.cancelled
                if not deadBefore
                    if not r.tapped and (r.bull ? low <= r.edge : high >= r.edge)
                        r.tapped := true
                        if (reqDisp and not r.dispFirst) or (reqFvg and not r.fvgFirst)
                            r.dropped := true
                    bool inv = invWick ? (r.bull ? low < r.tip : high > r.tip) : (r.bull ? close < r.tip : close > r.tip)
                    if inv
                        r.invalid := true
                        deadNow := true
                        invNow := true
                    if flatNow or bar_index - r.formBar > MAX_AGE
                        r.expired := true
                        deadNow := true
                if r.dropped
                    deleteDrawings(r)
                    r.resolved := true
                else
                    bool canFill = bar_index >= r.fillFrom
                    bool f0 = stepLimit(r.t0, r.bull, canFill, deadBefore, deadNow)
                    bool f1 = stepLimit(r.t1, r.bull, canFill, deadBefore, deadNow)
                    bool f2 = stepCisd(r.t2, r, canFill, deadBefore, deadNow, r.bull ? cisdBull : cisdBear, flatNow)
                    stepOpen(r.t0, r.bull, false, flatNow)
                    stepOpen(r.t1, r.bull, false, flatNow)
                    stepOpen(r.t2, r.bull, true, flatNow)
                    bool fSel = selIdx == 0 ? f0 : selIdx == 1 ? f1 : f2
                    if fSel
                        Trade ts = selTrade(r)
                        aFill := true
                        if not na(r.bx)
                            r.fillMk := label.new(bar_index, ts.entry, r.bull ? "▲" : "▼", color=color.new(color.black, 100), style=r.bull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, textcolor=colEnt, size=size.small)
                        alert((r.bull ? "Long" : "Short") + " RB entry (" + entrySel + ") @ " + str.tostring(ts.entry, format.mintick) + "  SL " + str.tostring(ts.stop, format.mintick) + "  TP1 " + str.tostring(ts.tp1, format.mintick) + "  TP2 " + str.tostring(ts.tp2, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
                    // only when the selected entry was still waiting and didn't fill on the way to the tip
                    if invNow and selLive and not tsI.filled
                        aInval := true
                        alert((r.bull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " RB invalidated (tip " + str.tostring(r.tip, format.mintick) + " taken)", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
                    Trade tsD = selTrade(r)
                    if r.resTxt == "" and isDone(tsD)
                        r.resTxt := not tsD.filled ? "no fill" : (tsD.r2 >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(tsD.r2, "0.0") + "R"
                        if not na(r.tag)
                            label.set_text(r.tag, tagText(r))
                            label.set_tooltip(r.tag, tagTip(r) + "\nResult (" + entrySel + ", held to TP2 on the same stop): " + r.resTxt)
                    if deadNow and not r.zoneDone
                        endZone(r)
                    if isDone(r.t0) and isDone(r.t1) and isDone(r.t2)
                        r.resolved := true
                        if not r.zoneDone
                            endZone(r)
                        countRB(r)
                        setups += 1
                    else if not r.zoneDone
                        if not na(r.bx)
                            box.set_right(r.bx, bar_index)
                        if not na(r.ceLn)
                            line.set_x2(r.ceLn, bar_index)

    // ---- build the RB-timeframe candle; finalize it on its last bar (A1)
    RB made1  = na
    RB made2  = na
    RB armed1 = na
    RB armed2 = na
    if not na(sHi)
        smtSeen := true
    if newRbBar
        if not aDone and not na(aO)
            [m1, a1] = finalize(aO, aH, aL, aC, aT, aBar, true, sAH, sAL)
            made1  := m1
            armed1 := a1
        aO    := open
        aH    := high
        aL    := low
        aC    := close
        aT    := time
        aBar  := bar_index
        aDone := false
        sAH   := sHi
        sAL   := sLo
    else if not na(aO)
        aH := math.max(aH, high)
        aL := math.min(aL, low)
        aC := close
        sAH := na(sAH) ? sHi : na(sHi) ? sAH : math.max(sAH, sHi)
        sAL := na(sAL) ? sLo : na(sLo) ? sAL : math.min(sAL, sLo)
    if lastRbBar and not aDone and not na(aO)
        [m2, a2] = finalize(aO, aH, aL, aC, aT, aBar, false, sAH, sAL)
        made2  := m2
        armed2 := a2
        aDone  := true

    for k = 0 to 1
        RB nr = k == 0 ? made1 : made2
        if not na(nr)
            drawNew(nr)
            array.push(rbs, nr)
            if nr.bull
                aNewBull := true
            else
                aNewBear := true
            alert((nr.bull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " RB [" + nr.grade + "] off " + nr.names + "  zone " + str.tostring(math.min(nr.tip, nr.edge), format.mintick) + " – " + str.tostring(math.max(nr.tip, nr.edge), format.mintick) + "  CE " + str.tostring(nr.ce, format.mintick) + "  SL " + str.tostring(nr.stop, format.mintick) + (nr.disp ? "  (displaced)" : ""), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
        RB ar = k == 0 ? armed1 : armed2
        if not na(ar)
            aArmed := true
            alert((ar.bull ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") + " RB displaced (CISD) before any touch: CE " + str.tostring(ar.ce, format.mintick) + "  SL " + str.tostring(ar.stop, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

    // ---- replaced levels go, and yesterday's key opens expire (A3)
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = array.size(lvls) - 1 to 0
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if not na(lv.deadT) or (lv.kind == 0 and lv.dayId < koDay)
                dropLvl(i)

    // ---- extend level lines
    if array.size(lvls) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(lvls) - 1
            Lvl lv = array.get(lvls, i)
            if not na(lv.ln)
                if bar_index - lv.bornBar > MAX_AGE
                    line.set_x1(lv.ln, bar_index - MAX_AGE)
                line.set_x2(lv.ln, bar_index)

    // ---- entry / stop / TP lines for the newest live RBs; only the newest maxKeep RBs
    // that are still drawn keep their drawings, and finished RBs with none are dropped
    int liveShown = 0
    int kept = 0
    int total = 0
    if array.size(rbs) > 0
        for i = array.size(rbs) - 1 to 0
            RB r = array.get(rbs, i)
            bool active = not r.resolved and not na(r.bx) and not isDone(selTrade(r))
            if active and liveShown < lvlN
                liveShown += 1
                drawTrade(r)
            else
                clearTrade(r)
            if not na(r.bx)
                kept += 1
                if kept > maxKeep
                    deleteDrawings(r)
            total += 1
            if na(r.bx) and (r.resolved or total > 300)
                array.remove(rbs, i)

// ============================== ALERTS =======================================
alertcondition(aNewBull, "Bullish RB formed", "Bullish rejection block formed")
alertcondition(aNewBear, "Bearish RB formed", "Bearish rejection block formed")
alertcondition(aArmed, "RB displaced (CISD)", "Rejection block displaced before its first touch")
alertcondition(aFill, "RB entry", "Rejection block entry filled/triggered")
alertcondition(aInval, "RB invalidated", "Rejection block invalidated before entry")

// ============================ STATS TABLE ====================================
var table stat = na
if barstate.islast and showStats
    tblPos = switch statsPos
        "Top Right"    => position.top_right
        "Top Left"     => position.top_left
        "Bottom Right" => position.bottom_right
        "Bottom Left"  => position.bottom_left
        "Middle Right" => position.middle_right
        => position.top_right
    if na(stat)
        stat := table.new(tblPos, 5, 21, border_width=1, frame_color=color.new(color.gray, 40), frame_width=1)
    else
        table.set_position(stat, tblPos)
    color hdrBg = color.new(color.gray, 20)
    color rowBg = color.new(color.black, 55)
    color txt   = color.white
    table.clear(stat, 0, 0, 4, 20)
    int live = 0
    if array.size(rbs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(rbs) - 1
            RB q = array.get(rbs, i)
            if not q.resolved
                live += 1

    table.cell(stat, 0, 0, "RB " + (rbTfIn == "Chart" ? timeframe.period : rbTfIn), bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 0, "Setups", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 0, str.tostring(setups), bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 0, "Live", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 4, 0, str.tostring(live), bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)

    // today's context: daily bias (A8) and the SMT partner (A11)
    int    bNow  = dayBias()
    string smtTx = not smtOn ? "off" : not smtSeen ? "no data" : array.last(str.split(smtSym, ":"))
    table.cell(stat, 0, 1, "Bias", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip=pxhBias ? "PXH/PXL: yesterday against the day before." : "The direction of yesterday's candle.")
    table.cell(stat, 1, 1, bNow == 1 ? "▲ Bull" : bNow == -1 ? "▼ Bear" : "– None", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=bNow == 1 ? colBull : bNow == -1 ? colBear : txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 1, "SMT", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 3, 1, smtTx, bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    string tfTip = "The RB timeframe is the chart timeframe, so fills are judged on the same candles: a candle that reaches the entry and then the stop counts as a loss even when the target came first. For fair stats, use a lower chart timeframe, e.g. a 1m chart with RB timeframe 5m."
    table.cell(stat, 4, 1, useAgg ? "" : "⚠ use a lower chart TF", bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=useAgg ? txt : colBear, text_size=size.small, tooltip=useAgg ? "" : tfTip)

    table.cell(stat, 0, 2, "Entry", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 1, 2, "Fills", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(stat, 2, 2, "Fill%", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Share of finished setups where this entry filled.")
    string tipTp = "Whole position held to that target with the same stop, no breakeven. Average R per filled trade · share of trades that ended above 0R."
    table.cell(stat, 3, 2, "→TP1", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip=tipTp)
    table.cell(stat, 4, 2, "→TP2", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip=tipTp)
    array<string> eNames = array.from("CE limit", "Body-edge limit", "CISD after tap")
    for m = 0 to 2
        int n = array.get(eFill, m)
        float s1 = array.get(eS1, m)
        float s2 = array.get(eS2, m)
        table.cell(stat, 0, 3 + m, (m == selIdx ? "▶ " : "") + array.get(eNames, m), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 1, 3 + m, str.tostring(n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 2, 3 + m, f_pct(n, setups), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 3, 3 + m, fR(s1, array.get(eW1, m), n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=n > 0 ? (s1 > 0 ? colBull : colBear) : txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 4, 3 + m, fR(s2, array.get(eW2, m), n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=n > 0 ? (s2 > 0 ? colBull : colBear) : txt, text_size=size.small)

    if fullTbl
        table.cell(stat, 0, 6, "Filter lab (▶)", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Fills of the selected entry (▶) where each filter held, whether or not it is required. Compare a row with All fills to see what that filter alone would change.")
        table.cell(stat, 1, 6, "N", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
        table.cell(stat, 2, 6, "Keep%", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip="Share of all fills this filter keeps.")
        table.cell(stat, 3, 6, "→TP1", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip=tipTp)
        table.cell(stat, 4, 6, "→TP2", bgcolor=hdrBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small, tooltip=tipTp)
        array<string> lNames = array.from("All fills", "Key level", "Killzone", "Premium/discount", "Daily bias", "Clean tip", "SMT", "Closed with rejection", "CISD first", "FVG first", "Grade A+", "Grade A", "Grade B", "Grade C")
        array<bool>   lReq   = array.from(false, reqKey, reqKz, reqPd, reqBias, reqClean, reqSmt, reqDir, reqDisp, reqFvg, false, false, false, false)
        int allN = array.get(lN, 0)
        for k = 0 to LAB_N - 1
            int n = array.get(lN, k)
            float s1 = array.get(lS1, k)
            float s2 = array.get(lS2, k)
            table.cell(stat, 0, 7 + k, array.get(lNames, k) + (array.get(lReq, k) ? " (req)" : ""), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
            table.cell(stat, 1, 7 + k, str.tostring(n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
            table.cell(stat, 2, 7 + k, f_pct(n, allN), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=txt, text_size=size.small)
            table.cell(stat, 3, 7 + k, fR(s1, array.get(lW1, k), n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=n > 0 ? (s1 > 0 ? colBull : colBear) : txt, text_size=size.small)
            table.cell(stat, 4, 7 + k, fR(s2, array.get(lW2, k), n), bgcolor=rowBg, text_color=n > 0 ? (s2 > 0 ? colBull : colBear) : txt, text_size=size.small)
